  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md Section 15 (0x1100-0x1128) per-field bit tables, cited by contract ID, and RCA-DFC-ARCH-002.md's dfc_rtl018_control_t/status_t Appendix B tables. Covers all 11 real ATX registers actually enumerated in REG-002 (see OPEN_ISSUES.md for the genuine REG-002-internal register-count discrepancy: Section 6's own Address-Map Summary says 11, Section 15's own block-header 'Register count' field says 12, and only 11 are ever defined -- resolved in favor of the 11 actually-enumerated registers, the only number with any real content behind it). ATX_DATA_STAGE/ATX_META_STAGE/ATX_CONTROL/ATX_PUSH/ATX_INTERWORD_GAP_BITS are plain RW/WO-CMD registers with readback class 'internal_reg'/'zero' -- the generic regbank already stores and returns their written value directly, so none of them need a status_registers entry, same precedent as RTL-017's own ARX_CONTROL/ARX_SNAPSHOT/ARX_POP. One real gap found and fixed while building this field map (the tenth real instance of the exact gap class already fixed for RTL-002 through RTL-017, approved before this session's edit): RTL018_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS.EVENT_OVERFLOW had no clear-forwarding control field at all in dfc_rtl018_control_t as ARCH-002 originally defined it. Fixed the same way as every prior instance: ARCH-002 grew dfc_rtl018_control_t 162->163 bits, adding rtl018_evt_overflow_status__event_overflow as a new clear_mask field at the new highest bit (162) -- every pre-existing field's bit position confirmed unchanged by direct comparison against the already-generated include/dfc_types_pkg.sv before this edit. See OPEN_ISSUES.md for the full disclosure.",
